# ShotBreakdown

Next.js 16 (App Router, React 19, Tailwind v4) + Supabase (auth, Postgres, storage) + Anthropic. Filmmakers paste a YouTube/TikTok link or upload a frame/clip and get a cinematography breakdown.

## Priority

1. Accurate, specific, actionable breakdowns for recreating a shot
2. Public SEO-indexable library of verified breakdowns
3. Calm UI — one clear action per screen
4. Async, safe, cheap backend
5. Flywheel: ratings, edits, saves, follow-ups improve prompts/retrieval and personalize

## Conventions

- TypeScript strict. Server Components by default; `"use client"` only where needed
- Zod for all API input/output validation
- Never trust client-supplied `user_id`; always `supabase.auth.getUser()`
- Keep black/zinc visual style. No new UI libraries
- Schema changes go in numbered files under `supabase/migrations/`
- Do not log secrets. Do not commit `.env.local`
- After each phase: `npm run lint && npx tsc --noEmit && npm run build` must pass
